  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Whiting Turner Contracting Company the obligated $1B in FY2026 to date across 70 awards, with an average award size of $14.5M. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the obligations are up 66.1% year over year. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the received most obligations from the Department of Homeland Security, which obligated $785M, followed by the Department of Defense, which obligated $216M. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the also recorded obligations with the General Services Administration at $25.7M, the National Gallery of Art at $11.7M, the Smithsonian Institution at $6.3M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $2.8M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest NAICS market for Whiting Turner Contracting Company the with $1B in obligations. Historical annual obligations were $730M in FY21, $355M in FY22, $675M in FY23, $503M in FY24, and $611M in FY25.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest federal buyers of Whiting Turner Contracting Company the?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the biggest buyer, obligating $785M to Whiting Turner Contracting Company the in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer, obligating $216M. The General Services Administration and cultural agencies follow, with $25.7M for the General Services Administration and $11.7M for the National Gallery of Art."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What work is Whiting Turner Contracting Company the doing for the government?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the primary market for Whiting Turner Contracting Company the with $1B in obligations. All Other Specialty Trade Contractors is a secondary market with $11.7M in obligations. Whiting Turner Contracting Company the has delivered smaller projects for the Smithsonian Institution at $6.3M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $2.8M."
      }
    ]
